Q: HTML and CSS Change Date Formatting On Whole Web Page A: <p>I would wrap all dates in a <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/q/6852866/901048"><code>&lt;time&gt;</code> element</a>, then use JavaScript to convert that to a <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/q/85116/901048">local date format</a>.</p>

<p>HTML:</p>

<pre><code>Published &lt;time datetime="2011-07-03"&gt;07/03&lt;/time&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>JS:</p>

<pre><code>var elements = document.getElementsByTagName("time");
for (var i=0; i&lt;elements.length; i++) {
    var dat = new Date('UTC:'+elements[i].getAttribute('datetime'));
    elements[i].innerHTML = dat.toLocaleDateString();
}
</code></pre>

